# KING TODO map
# TODO:
# [ ] FROM debian:bookworm-slim as base — minimal OS, no build tools
# [ ] ARG KING_VERSION — injected by Buck2 build, renovate regex manager tracks it
# [ ] COPY buck-out/gen/base/mint/king /usr/local/bin/rice-king — pre-built binary
# [ ] COPY .cursor/rules/KING.mdc /etc/rice/rules/KING.mdc — role MDC injected at runtime
# [ ] COPY .cursor/rules/*.mdc /etc/rice/rules/ — KING reads all role MDCs
# [ ] ENV RICE_ROLE=king
# [ ] ENV RICE_RULES_DIR=/etc/rice/rules
# [ ] ENV RICE_MCP_FILESYSTEM_ROOT=/ — KING filesystem MCP reads entire container
# [ ] HEALTHCHECK: rice-king --health-check with interval RICE_KING_HEALTH_INTERVAL
# [ ] USER rice — non-root, UID/GID soft-coded via ARG RICE_UID RICE_GID
# [ ] no ENTRYPOINT script — binary is the entrypoint
#     rice-king is invoked by `rice rule` dispatch from Justfile
# [ ] KING never runs as a daemon — it is invoked per task
